# CODEOWNERS.example — copy to .github/CODEOWNERS and replace the placeholders.
# This file is intentionally inert: GitHub only reads .github/CODEOWNERS.
# Use real @user or @org/team handles that have write access. Do NOT commit
# placeholder handles to the real CODEOWNERS file; unknown owners are ignored/invalid.
# Later matching patterns take precedence over earlier ones.

# Repository-wide default owner
# *                           @ORG/TEAM-NAME

# Governance and AI contract (require review from people accountable for team policy)
# /AGENTS.md                  @ORG/TEAM-GOVERNANCE
# **/AGENTS.md                @ORG/TEAM-GOVERNANCE
# /.ai/                       @ORG/TEAM-GOVERNANCE
# /SECURITY.md                @ORG/TEAM-SECURITY
# /CONTRIBUTING.md            @ORG/TEAM-GOVERNANCE

# CI/CD configuration
# /.github/                   @ORG/TEAM-PLATFORM

# Security-sensitive files
# /docs/security/             @ORG/TEAM-SECURITY

# Infrastructure
# /infrastructure/            @ORG/TEAM-INFRA

# Architecture and decisions
# /docs/architecture/         @ORG/TEAM-ARCHITECTS
# /docs/decisions/            @ORG/TEAM-ARCHITECTS

# Shared libraries
# /libs/                      @ORG/TEAM-SHARED-LIBS
